  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Chandrashekar N Shetty @ Chandrashekar vs Suresh Kumar C on 8 February, 2024 Author: Pradeep Singh Yerur Bench: Pradeep Singh Yerur -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:5384 Mfa No. 5528 of 2021 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 8Th Day Of February, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Pradeep Singh Yerur Miscellaneous First Appeal No.5528 Of 2021(Mv-I) Between: Chandrashekar N.Shetty @ Chandrashekar, S/O Narasimha Shetty, Aged About 39 Years, R/At No.659, 4Th Cross, 5Th Main, Bommanahalli, Begur Road, Bengaluru-560 068. ...Appellant (By Sri. A.Sreenivasaiah, Advocate) Digitally And: signed by Gayathri P G 1. Suresh Kumar C., Location: High S/O Chidambaram, Court of Karnataka No.222, 1St Floor, 5Th Main Road, Singasandra, Hosur Main Road, Bengaluru-560 068. 2. The Manager, Reliance General Insurance Co. Ltd., 5Th Floor, Centenary Building, No.28, M.G.Road, Bengaluru-560 001. ...RESPONDENTS (VIDE ORDER DATED 22.11.2022, SRI.B.PRADEEP, ADVOCATE FOR R2 (VAKALAT NOT FILED); Chandrashekar N Shetty @ Chandrashekar vs Suresh Kumar C on 8 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/52045495/ 1 NOTICE TO R1 DISPENSED WITH; SRI. ASHOK N.PATIL, ADVOCATE FOR R2) THIS MFA FILED U/S.173(1) OF MV ACT, AGAINST THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED 25.02.2021 IN MVC NO.2710/2019 ON THE FILE OF THE VIII ADDITIONAL SMALL -2- NC: 2024:KHC:5384 MFA No. 5528 of 2021 CAUSES JUDGE AND ACMM, MEMBER, MACT, BENGALURU, (SCCH-5), PARTLY ALLOWING THE CLAIM PETITION FOR COMPENSATION AND SEEKING ENHANCEMENT OF COMPENSATION. THIS APPEAL, COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS DAY, THE COURT DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: JUDGMENT",
    "facts": "This appeal is founded on the premise of inadequacy and meager compensation awarded by the Tribunal. Hence, the appellants seek for enhancement of compensation. 2. Parties to the appeal shall be referred to as per their status before the Tribunal. Due to the said impact, claimant sustained grievous injuries. Immediately, he was shifted to Kavya Hospital, Bengaluru, wherein, first aid treatment was given. 3.1 On service of notice, respondent No.1 did not appeared before the Court and he was placed ex-parte. Respondent No.2-Insurance Company appeared before the Court and filed statement of objection denying the claim of the claimant including age, avocation, income and negligence attributed against the driver of the offending vehicle and sought for dismissal of the claim petition. 3.4 On the basis of material evidence, both oral and documentary and on hearing the submissions of learned counsel for both parties, the tribunal has awarded the compensation of Rs.4,05,000/- with interest at 9% per annum from the date of petition till its realization and respondent No.2-Insurance Company is liable to pay the compensation to the claimant and directed to deposit the said amount within 60 days from the date of the order.",
    "arguments": "The main contention of the learned counsel for the appellant-claimant that the tribunal has committed an error in awarding meager compensation and it has not taken into consideration the avocation, age and the magnitude of the injuries sustained by the claimant due to road traffic accident. The tribunal has not awarded reasonable compensation under other heads also. Accordingly, he seeks to allow the appeal preferred by the claimant and seeks enhancement of compensation. 5. Per contra, learned counsel for respondent- Insurance Company submits that the tribunal has rightly awarded just and reasonable compensation, which does not call for interference. Therefore, on these grounds, he seeks to dismiss the appeal."
  },
